<title>USA: Arvin, Kayaba form pump venture.</title>
<headline>Arvin, Kayaba form pump venture.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ind. 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arvin Industries Inc said it and Kayaba Industry Co Ltd of Japan agreed to form a joint venture to manufacture and sell power steering pumps to European car makers.</p>
<p>The new company, Kayaba Arvin SA, is based in a new plant in Pamplona, Spain, and will begin production in 1997.</p>
<p>Kayaba will own 60 percent of the new company's shares and Arvin, 40 percent.</p>
<p>Kayaba is a power steering pump producer. Arvin is an international manufacturer of automotive components.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
